        "date": "2026-11-11T07:03:07Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post,machine): Tormach microARC 4 - A indexing in the PathPilot post\n\nA new machine file, Tormach 770MX + microARC 4, states an A rotary about\nX (travel -360..360 degrees, rates unstated; TD10749). The PathPilot post\nindexes A between operations: G53 G0 Z to the safe Z, then G0 A alone at a\nsection's first motion, and writes each indexed section's tips in the\nturned frame (relative to the work offset, turned by -A about X). The A\nword is read through the tool axis, so the pose law's A0 B180 posts as\nA180. The direction sense is the sign of the rotary's axis vector. A\nmachine with an A states it at its first motion (A0 for upright work).\n\nRefused by name: a tilt the A axis cannot reach (any X component, any\nC), an A past the stated travel, an A that changes inside an operation\n(simultaneous 4-axis - rollover and combined feed unconfirmed on\nPathPilot, #796), an arc on an indexed A, and a tilt on a machine with no\nA about X. No clamp code is written (none exists on the microARC 4).\n\nAlso fixes parse_mch's head search, which stopped at the first leaf part\nand dropped the spindle, belt ranges and coolant of any file with a leaf\nahead of its head.\n\nAdds the microARC hardware test kit (docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th:\nREADME, the app-built project and its posted program, pinned by\nmicroarc_test_part.rs).\n\nRefs #785\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
