      "message": "fix(post): restate A after every G30 on the microARC 4 (review of PR #798)\n\nThe bare G30 before every T.. M6 moves every axis to the stored G30\nposition under LinuxCNC (params 5181-5189), A included, but the post kept\nthe A word it last wrote and skipped the index when the next section sat\non the same face. Two operations on one face (a rough and a finish at\nA90, or T3 then T4) posted the second with no G0 A.., cutting wherever\nG30 left the table.\n\nThe post now forgets the held A when it writes G30, and at every section\nend, so every section opens with G53 G0 Z / G0 A.. - a same-tool\ncontinuation too (a section boundary is where an operator may stop and\njog). The 4-face golden and the kit program are unchanged: every op\nthere indexed already.\n\nPinned by a_tool_change_on_the_same_face_restates_a_after_the_g30 and\na_same_tool_continuation_on_the_same_face_restates_a (both fail before).\n\nAlso: the kit README warns that the safe Z is the top of travel (confirm\nthe part/chuck/jaw swept radius clears the tool there) and that each G30\ncan move A; checklist item 7 no longer claims A ends at 0. The parser's\nhead search gets a direct test (mch_head_search.rs), and find_type's doc\ncomment is back on find_type.\n\nRefs #785\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
