      "message": "feat(app): refuse an A index whose retracted tool can't clear the swept work\n\nBefore a 4th axis that turns the work indexes, the post lifts Z to the\nsafe retract and turns A under the tool. The program gate now checks\nthat the tool tip there clears the radius the stock, the parts and the\nturning fixtures sweep about the A centerline, with a 5 mm margin, and\nrefuses the post by name otherwise (op, A, tip height, swept radius,\nclearance).\n\n- .mch: a work-turning rotary (no head below it) may state nose_to_axis,\n  the spindle nose's height above its centerline at safe_retract. The\n  microARC 4 file states 10.6 in (770MX 13.75 in nose to table less the\n  microARC's 3.15 in centre height). Unstated on a work-turning A about\n  X refuses by name.\n- posting::index_swing: the gate clause; machines with no work-turning A\n  (and head tilts) are untouched.\n- The tester-kit .camproj is re-saved with the new machine facts; the kit\n  .nc is byte-identical.\n\nFixes #804\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
