      "message": "fix(app): judge a table A with no axis vector; name pre-#804 machines on load\n\nFollow-ups to the #804 index-swing check (PR #810 review):\n\n- A work-turning rotary with no axis vector was not judged, a silent\n  pass. It now takes its RS-274 letter's line: an A is about X and is\n  judged like the microARC's. One with no vector and no RS-274 rotary\n  letter refuses every op by name, asking for its axis.\n- AxisLimits::turns_part is Option<bool>: a parsed rotary always states\n  it, so a rotary read back without the key was saved before #804.\n  Opening such a project adds a load note naming the machine and the\n  rotary and asking for the machine to be reloaded.\n- The microARC tester kit README says to keep the stored G30 Z at the\n  top of travel; assets/machines/AGENTS.md documents the axis rule.\n- Decision record: docs/decisions/813-swing-gaps.md.\n\nFixes #813\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
